      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. it's a good start, but honestly, it feels a bit thin for a board-level report. even though you mentioned staying concise, the board is going to want to see much more granular detail on the specific failures. \n\nthe current summary is only 4 bullets/points. i really need this to look substantial so they don't think we missed things. can you expand this out? try to break down the findings into much more specific, detailed sub-points—especially regarding the documentation issues, the training gaps, and the digital interface. i need the audit to look \"dense\" with information. \n\nagain, pls don't just repeat yourself, but i definitely need a much higher level of granularity and a much higher bullet count than what you just gave me to make this look professional and thorough.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
